--TEST--
Off a request, `Core\Response::sendSlotted()` in the main script does not throw, and in `Core\Task::runAfterResponse` work it throws `LogicError`, because the main script has ended -- `rule:core-classes/html-later`
--FILE--
<?nvs
Core\Response::sendSlotted();
echo "main\n";

// This work runs after the script ends, so the call throws `LogicError`.
// The work is in a variable, so the compiler does not see the call.
var $work = fn(): void => {
    try {
        Core\Response::sendSlotted();
    } catch (LogicError $e) {
        echo $e->message, "\n";
    }
};
Core\Task::runAfterResponse($work);
--EXPECT--
main
`Core\Response::sendSlotted()` was called after the main script ended. Call it before the main script returns.
